mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><strong>Optometry</strong>&nbsp;is a medical discipline dedicated primarily to the protection of human visual health. This course covers the most essential and prominent clinical issues in optometry, including fundamental physiology and anatomy, refractive errors, visual dysfunctions, and low-vision rehabilitation. It provides an understanding of various areas such as spectacle dispensing, contact lens fitting, myopia control, management of binocular vision disorders, and refractive surgery. Through practical learning, students will experience the essential professional skills required for an optometrist.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
